This version loads `profile` and `profileIndex` into locals once. The original repeats member reads that the compiler may not be able to merge because of possible aliasing, so this removes redundant loads. Behavior is identical: the same NULL and bounds checks run, and the same values are returned.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    const FIT_UINT16 idx = profileIndex;
    if ((p == NULL) || (idx >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[idx].num;
}
```